1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,613
Good morning and
thank you for tuning in to

2
00:00:02,637 --> 00:00:05,332
this recorded talk on
how recycling and waste

3
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,419
collection work in our
area. Let's start with

4
00:00:08,443 --> 00:00:11,680
what goes where. Bottles
and jars made of glass

5
00:00:11,681 --> 00:00:14,376
have their own bin,
the one with the blue lid.

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,872
Please don't put glass
in with your paper.

7
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:20,314
Grass cuttings, leaves
and hedge trimmings all

8
00:00:20,338 --> 00:00:23,387
go in the brown bin. A
lot of people throw broken

9
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:26,377
kettles and toasters in
with their general rubbish.

10
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:29,287
Please don't. Anything
electrical has to be taken

11
00:00:29,288 --> 00:00:31,681
to the recycling
centre on Mill Road.

12
00:00:31,705 --> 00:00:35,814
Plastic bottles are fine but
plastic bags are a different story.

13
00:00:35,815 --> 00:00:38,341
Our machines can't
process them so at the

14
00:00:38,365 --> 00:00:41,677
moment there is simply no
way to recycle them locally.

15
00:00:41,678 --> 00:00:43,839
As for food scraps
and peelings, many

16
00:00:43,863 --> 00:00:46,632
people think these belong
with the garden waste

17
00:00:46,869 --> 00:00:49,376
but they actually go
in with your paper and

18
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,212
cardboard in the green
bin. Now, collection days

19
00:00:52,374 --> 00:00:54,885
because these have
changed recently.

20
00:00:54,909 --> 00:00:58,215
The green bin goes out
first thing on a Monday.

21
00:00:58,216 --> 00:01:01,731
Glass is collected mid-week on
Wednesday. The brown bin used

22
00:01:01,755 --> 00:01:04,891
to be collected on a Tuesday
but it's now picked up at

23
00:01:04,892 --> 00:01:07,935
the end of the week, on
Friday. Some households

24
00:01:07,959 --> 00:01:11,092
have been given a small
separate caddy for food.

25
00:01:11,379 --> 00:01:14,267
That's emptied on the
same day as the green bin.

26
00:01:14,291 --> 00:01:17,432
And general rubbish has
also moved. It was a Tuesday

27
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:21,010
collection but it's now
Thursday. Next, items that

28
00:01:21,034 --> 00:01:24,480
don't belong in any of
your bins. For batteries,

29
00:01:24,481 --> 00:01:27,423
you don't need to go all
the way to the council depot.

30
00:01:27,447 --> 00:01:31,162
Most supermarkets now have a
collection point out in their car park.

31
00:01:31,163 --> 00:01:35,472
Unwanted clothes are gladly accepted
by the charity shops on the high street.

32
00:01:36,009 --> 00:01:39,130
Furniture, of course, is far
too bulky for the supermarket.

33
00:01:39,154 --> 00:01:41,087
That has to go to
the council depot.

34
00:01:41,088 --> 00:01:43,748
Printer cartridges are
collected by several local

35
00:01:43,772 --> 00:01:47,069
schools which raise money by
sending them off for recycling.

36
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:49,802
And engine oil must
never go down the drain.

37
00:01:49,826 --> 00:01:52,052
Take it to a petrol
station instead.

38
00:01:52,053 --> 00:01:55,164
Finally, a word about
why all this matters.

39
00:01:55,188 --> 00:01:59,600
People sometimes say composting
saves them money. And it may.

40
00:01:59,601 --> 00:02:02,537
But the real point is
that it reduces landfill.

41
00:02:02,561 --> 00:02:05,807
The car sharing scheme
means fewer cars on the road,

42
00:02:05,808 --> 00:02:09,116
which reduces emissions.
That's why the council supports

43
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:12,052
it. The bring your own
bag scheme helps wildlife,

44
00:02:12,390 --> 00:02:14,988
because fewer bags end
up in rivers and the sea.

45
00:02:15,012 --> 00:02:17,727
The deposits from the can
and bottle return scheme

46
00:02:17,728 --> 00:02:20,031
raise funds for
schools in the area.

47
00:02:20,055 --> 00:02:23,652
And energy-saving light
bulbs do cut emissions slightly,

48
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:27,320
but the main benefit households
notice is that they save money.

49
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:29,703
Thank you for listening,
and please do your

50
00:02:29,727 --> 00:02:32,292
part to help our town
recycle more effectively.

